    "answered_by": "live-marker",
    "reason": "Ownership is read from markers stamped on live resources (Kubernetes labels `chant.intentius.io/stack`). Chant has no authoritative state file; the invariant is 'The projection reads ownership from the live marker, never from the snapshot.'"
  },
  "q3": "newly-observed",
  "q4": {
    "action": "adopt",
    "reason": "An undeclared orphan with no ownership marker is classified adopt (candidate to pull into source), never automatic delete. Delete is only proposed when the live marker confirms the resource belongs to this stack."
  },
  "q5": {
    "calls_cloud": false,
    "reason": "chant build stays pure: it parses TypeScript, evaluates resource definitions, and serializes output. No credentials are consulted; no network calls to AWS or Kubernetes APIs occur. Only I/O is reading source files and writing output."
  },
  "q6": {
    "requires_controller_reconcile": false,
    "reason": "Snapshot only requires declared entities to exist and be GET-able via the k8s API server. CAPI/CAPA controllers need not have actually provisioned real EKS infrastructure; the Kubernetes objects themselves suffice to record PRESENT status."
  },
  "q7": {
    "specific_to_k8s_lexicon": true,
    "reason": "K8s lexicon's describeResources() records only identity-depth attributes (namespace, labels, resourceVersion) with no reference-catalog enrichment step, so --at/--live graphs yield zero edges. AWS lexicon has this enrichment; declared graphs (offline, no --at/--live) are unaffected."
  }
